---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../config';

// Order follows the tatami pinwheel: top, right, bottom, left.
const mat = [
  { id: 'dairy', name: 'Dairy production data', where: 'Tetra Pak', fill: 'hakama' },
  { id: 'sustainability', name: 'Sustainability recommendations', where: 'Tetra Pak', fill: 'lichen' },
  { id: 'talent', name: 'Talent matching', where: 'Accelerated Growth AB', fill: 'hakama' },
  { id: 'ikea', name: 'Engineering management', where: 'IKEA', fill: 'lichen' },
];
---
<Base
  title="Work"
  description="Enterprise AI and data engineering. Dairy production data and sustainability systems at Tetra Pak, engineering management at IKEA."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1 class="display">Work</h1>
      <div class="column prose intro">
        <p class="lede">
          I've spent fifteen years between engineering and the people who have to decide things.
          The technical half is data platforms, pipelines and AI systems. The other half is sitting
          with the people who own the problem until the requirement is actually a requirement and
          not a wish.
        </p>
        <p>Currently placed at Tetra Pak through Accelerated Growth AB.</p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <nav class="mat" aria-label="Engagements on this page">
      {mat.map((m, i) => (
        <a class={`mat__block mat__block--${i + 1} fill-${m.fill}`} href={`#${m.id}`}>
          <span class="mat__name">{m.name}</span>
          <span class="mat__where">{m.where}</span>
        </a>
      ))}
      <span class="mat__center" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </nav>

    <article class="case" id="dairy" aria-labelledby="dairy-h">
      <p class="label">Tetra Pak</p>
      <h2 id="dairy-h" class="headline">Dairy production data</h2>
      <div class="column prose">
        <p>
          A dairy operation generates data at every stage: collection, separation, pasteurisation,
          whey streams, cheese, filling and packing. Each stage has its own systems and its own
          people. Very few can see across all of them at once.
        </p>
        <p>
          I work across that chain as a data engineer and developer. Pipelines that bring the stages
          into one place, dashboards that operations teams actually open, and machine learning
          models and AI reporting built on top of the result.
        </p>
      </div>
      <dl class="field column">
        <dt>Built with</dt>
        <dd>Azure Databricks, Unity Catalog, Lakeflow, Databricks SQL, MLflow, Power BI.</dd>
      </dl>
    </article>

    <article class="case" id="sustainability" aria-labelledby="sust-h">
      <p class="label">Tetra Pak</p>
      <h2 id="sust-h" class="headline">Sustainability recommendations</h2>
      <div class="column prose">
        <p>
          Two problems landing on one department. The sustainability specialists knew there were
          improvements available across customers' production lines that nobody was finding
          systematically. They were also answering every specialist question coming from a sales
          organisation working across more than 160 countries.
        </p>
        <p>
          I built a recommendation engine that identifies sustainability options for a given
          customer, covering both changes to the production line and broader measures like solar.
          And a chatbot trained on internal sustainability material, so the global team can get
          answers on specialist subjects without routing every question through a department that
          was never going to scale to meet them.
        </p>
      </div>
      <dl class="field column">
        <dt>Built with</dt>
        <dd>Azure Databricks, Power BI, Dash, Azure AI Foundry with RAG over internal sustainability material.</dd>
      </dl>
    </article>

    <article class="case" id="talent" aria-labelledby="talent-h">
      <p class="label">Accelerated Growth AB</p>
      <h2 id="talent-h" class="headline">Talent matching</h2>
      <div class="column prose">
        <p>
          Our commercial inbox was the bottleneck. Every assignment request arriving needed
          evaluating against what we could actually staff, and once it qualified, someone had to
          work through the consultant database weighing availability, location, skills and where
          that person wanted their career to go. It isn't work that gets faster by adding people to
          it.
        </p>
        <p>
          I built a system that reads the inbox, qualifies incoming requests and ranks consultants
          against them on those criteria. It cut a process measured in hours down to minutes.
        </p>
        <p>This is the one I can show in detail, because it's ours rather than a client's.</p>
      </div>
      <dl class="field column">
        <dt>Built with</dt>
        <dd>Azure Logic Apps, deployed models.</dd>
      </dl>
    </article>

    <article class="case" id="ikea" aria-labelledby="ikea-h">
      <p class="label">IKEA</p>
      <h2 id="ikea-h" class="headline">Engineering management</h2>
      <div class="column prose">
        <p>
          Engineering management and vendor strategy for the platforms behind IKEA's
          organisation-wide surveys. Line management of a software engineering team, four suppliers
          across different products and services, budget ownership, and the integration work to
          make several separately-bought solutions behave like one thing.
        </p>
        <p>
          Less AI than the rest of this page, and more of what makes AI projects actually land:
          getting engineers, suppliers and product management pointed at the same outcome before
          anyone writes code.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <section class="case together" aria-labelledby="together-h">
      <h2 id="together-h" class="headline">Working together</h2>
      <div class="column prose">
        <p>
          I take on data platform work, AI system design and the discovery that has to happen
          before either. Available through Accelerated Growth AB or directly, depending on the
          shape of the engagement.
        </p>
        <p class="together__mail"><a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .intro {
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
  }

  /* The mat: four 2:1 blocks in a pinwheel around a square centre,
     so no four corners meet. Stacks on narrow screens. */
  .mat {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-1);
    margin-block: var(--space-8) var(--space-12);
  }

  .mat__block {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: flex-end;
    gap: var(--space-1);
    min-height: 7rem;
    padding: var(--space-4);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .mat__name {
    font: var(--title);
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .mat__where {
    font: var(--small);
  }

  .fill-hakama {
    background: var(--hakama);
    color: var(--on-hakama);
  }

  .fill-lichen {
    background: var(--lichen);
    color: var(--on-lichen);
  }

  .mat__block:hover {
    color: inherit;
  }

  .mat__block:hover .mat__name {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-thickness: var(--stroke-hair);
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
  }

  .fill-hakama:hover {
    color: var(--on-hakama);
  }

  .fill-lichen:hover {
    color: var(--on-lichen);
  }

  .mat__center {
    display: none;
  }

  @media (min-width: 720px) {
    .mat {
      max-width: 36rem;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
      grid-template-rows: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      aspect-ratio: 1;
    }

    .mat__block {
      min-height: 0;
    }

    .mat__block--1 {
      grid-column: 1 / 3;
      grid-row: 1;
    }

    .mat__block--2 {
      grid-column: 3;
      grid-row: 1 / 3;
    }

    .mat__block--3 {
      grid-column: 2 / 4;
      grid-row: 3;
    }

    .mat__block--4 {
      grid-column: 1;
      grid-row: 2 / 4;
    }

    .mat__center {
      display: block;
      grid-column: 2;
      grid-row: 2;
      background: var(--mark);
    }
  }

  .case {
    border-top: var(--stroke-hair) solid var(--line);
    padding-block: var(--space-8) var(--space-12);
    scroll-margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }

  .case h2 {
    margin: var(--space-1) 0 var(--space-8);
  }

  .case .field {
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
  }

  .together__mail {
    font: var(--title);
  }
</style>
